Thanks Kent! On appeasement "value," it's my understanding
from wikihack that value is usually roughly the difficulty of the
sacrificed monster, and that a sacrifice's value determines
how much the sac:
1) reduces your God's anger
2) reduces your prayer timeout
3) increases your luck if you didn't get an artifact
as applicable (if Lugh isn't angry, fall through to 2;
if you can safely pray, fall through to 3).

So if I'm reading this correctly, a cross-aligned unicorn is
as valuable to sacrifice as say a troll or glass piercer,
whereas ordinarily it would be just as valuable as a
dwarf king or iron piercer.

Also, the alignment bonus probably isn't a big deal; since
it's my understanding that your alignment will usually be
high enough for anything you want to accomplish, unless
you're doing some conduct that likely precludes you from
sacrificing unicorns anyway, or you like beating up on
quest friendlies or fighting exclusively with poison arrows
as a samurai. So the benefit for saccing unicorns would
seem to be mostly for style points.


